# Invariants & contracts
  @invariant  sole truth for valid keys; in-code access raises on unknowns, loaded unknowns pruned  @ 3
  @invariant  owns cache: reads deep-clone out, writes deep-clone in; callers never alias cm state  @ 4
  @invariant  5-tier merge: global→project→track→take→transient; most-specific wins, else defaults  @ 5
  @invariant  transient tier never persists (saver is a no-op) and resets to {} on every refreshCache  @ 6
  @invariant  declarations is ordered array-of-pairs; nil-default keys coexist with non-nil defaults  @ 7
  @invariant  track/take tiers require REAPER context; without it loaders return {}, savers error  @ 8
  @contract  caches lazy: first getter triggers refreshCache; setContext/setTrack refresh eagerly  @ 325
  @contract  no take context drops track too (track derived from take in setContext)  @ 326
  @contract  deep-copy of resolved value (most-specific tier, else default); raises on unknown key  @ 493
  @contract  opts.mergeTiers=true → per-subkey union across defaults+tiers; table-valued keys only  @ 494
  @contract  opts.pick=<subkey> → indexes the resolved value before copying; nil when absent  @ 495

# Shapes
  @shape  configChangedPayload.targeted = { key = string, level = string }   -- set / remove  @ 9
  @shape  configChangedPayload.bulk     = { level = string }                  -- assign (keyless)  @ 10
  @shape  configChangedPayload.reload   = {}                                  -- setContext / clearTake / setTrack  @ 11

